.TH ANONYX 1 "2026-09-23" "anonyx 3.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
anonyx \- fail-closed Tor killswitch for Debian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anonyx
\fB--enable\fR [\fB--mode strict|paranoid|transparent\fR]
.br
.B anonyx
\fB--restore\fR | \fB--disable\fR | \fB--status\fR | \fB--leaktest\fR | \fB--audit\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
nftables-first (iptables fallback) killswitch. DNS to Tor only, IPv6 off,
optional Tor network-namespace isolation with fwmark policy routing.
Verifies exit via Tor API, logs to append-only audit log, restores from
/run/tor-killswitch/state.json without reboot.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/tor-killswitch/config
.br
.I /run/tor-killswitch/state.json
.br
.I /var/log/tor-killswitch/audit.log
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tor (1),
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables (8)
.SH WARNINGS
ISP still sees Tor usage. No malware or fingerprinting protection.
Do not run Tor Browser on top (Tor-over-Tor).
